          "occurrence_id": "29:41/r08",
          "branch_key": "root_001687/B001",
          "role": "Loss of strength exposes the shelter's failure under protective load."
        }
      ],
      "structural_cues": [
        "The same verb of taking governs both patrons and the spider's house, while house is repeated and ranked as weakest."
      ],
      "reader_inference": "The packet supplies adopted patrons, a constructed house, and structural weakness; I infer that beautification misreports the reliability of the whole deed-and-affiliation system. The live alternative is that the simile concerns patrons alone and does not reactivate the focus's dwellings or deeds.",
      "changed_reading": {
        "before": "Beautification simply makes objectionable deeds look pleasant.",
        "after": "Beautification falsifies structural judgment, causing vulnerable dependencies and practices to feel like a load-bearing home."
      }
    },
    {
      "model_id": "delta_counterpractice_reverses_blockage",
      "status": "revised",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "mechanism": "The focus has adorned deeds blocking agents from a route; established prayer is said to restrain conspicuous wrong, while remembrance refreshes awareness. These are inverse behavioral gates: repeated practice, not sight alone, determines which stream of action is inhibited.",
