        {
          "occurrence_id": "29:60/r03",
          "branch_key": "root_000560/B001",
          "role": "An apportioned gift relocates subsistence from local control to divine giving."
        }
      ],
      "structural_cues": [
        "The late sequence moves from wide earth to divinely assigned chambers and then to creatures that do not carry their own provision."
      ],
      "reader_inference": "The packet supplies a residence-fixing provision branch, spatial breadth, new lodging, and uncarrried divine provision; I infer that dependence on locally secured livelihood can cause immobility and that trust releases it. The live alternative is that the later reassurance addresses persecution and anxiety generally rather than explaining the focus peoples.",
      "changed_reading": {
        "before": "The dwellings are only post-destruction evidence.",
        "after": "They can also warn how locally secured comfort and livelihood immobilize agents, whereas released dependence permits movement and eventual re-housing."
      }
    },
    {
      "model_id": "delta_state_dependent_lucidity",
      "status": "revised",
      "confidence": "strong",
      "mechanism": "Correct recognition can coexist with being turned; ship-danger produces purified allegiance, rescue is followed by renewed association, and secure conditions surround belief in falsehood. Mustabṣirīn can therefore describe real but state-dependent lucidity rather than durable orientation.",
